poem:
He hunner yurs ol' an' nebber wuz ill;
He hurled the world;
And Georgie--none could ever dive like
him--
But when the cyclone
Breathes terror through the eternity of

Sailing the seven seas;
He will go down to hell.
I'm out to be wooed;
And browse about our ancient place,
Lay the victims of the dying stars.
Symbolic mother, we thy myriad

Where war has sharpened his weapons,
Stood frowning there, a cave here, bred
six
Who made the gallows an altar high,
Thy signals, ever and anon she cried;
But would please the weak frail flesh;
